<title>INDIA: India soybean, soyoil continue firm on poor supply.</title>
<headline>India soybean, soyoil continue firm on poor supply.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices continued firm in central Indian markets on Monday on poor arrivals.</p>
<p>Demand from processing plants was good. Soyoil was also firm on tight supply from plants and refineries.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady in very thin trading as availability was very poor.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was $318-320 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $118-120 per tonne in export and was 4,200 rupees per tonne in FOR condition.</p>
